// An edit block's value is the function its commit gives back, not the last expression its body
// writes (graph-editing design 6 and 15.1): this body ends with an int, and the block is still the
// function, so it type-checks where that function type is expected. The types are written out
// rather than left to a type parameter, so that what the case pins is the block and nothing else.
// The `!` is the block's: it is the function its commit gives, or the error that stopped the commit.
func value_is_the_function(f: (x: float) => float) => ((x: float) => float)! {
    return edit d = f { 42 }
}